                    facts: [
                        "A whole-step bend goes up two frets' worth. A half step is one fret.",
                        "Bend with finger 3. Put fingers 1 and 2 behind it on the same string to help push.",
                        "Turn your wrist like a doorknob. Don't push with one fingertip.",
                    ],
                    visual: Some(Tab([(string: 3, fret: 7, tech: Some(Bend(2)), beats: 2.0), (string: 3, fret: 5), (string: 4, fret: 7, beats: 2.0)])),
                ),
                Learn(
                    title: "Three sweet bend spots",
                    explain: "Here is a trick to bend in tune. First play the goal note two frets higher. Listen to it. Then go back and bend until you match it. Box 1 has three great spots to bend.",
                    facts: [
                        "String 3, fret 7 (D): bend up to E.",
                        "String 2, fret 8 (G): bend up to A, the root.",
                        "String 1, fret 8 (C): bend up to D.",
                        "On an acoustic guitar, start with half-step bends. Electric strings bend easier.",
                    ],
                    visual: Some(Neck(notes: [(string: 3, fret: 7), (string: 2, fret: 8), (string: 1, fret: 8)], first_fret: 4, last_fret: 10, show_names: true)),
                ),
                Learn(
                    title: "Check your bend",
                    explain: "A bend should land on a real note. Here's a trick. First play fret 9 on string 3 and listen. Then bend fret 7 until it sounds the same. If it's too low, push more. If it's too high, push less.",
                    facts: [
                        "A whole-step bend sounds like two frets higher.",
                        "Fret 7 bent up a whole step sounds like fret 9.",
                    ],
                    tips: [
                        "Use three fingers to push! Put fingers 1 and 2 behind finger 3 to help.",
                        "Turn your wrist like turning a doorknob. Don't just push with the fingertip.",
